10:59.180 --> 11:02.980
Ah. So the algorithm loses its ability to distinguish between the variables.

11:03.360 --> 11:05.320
Yeah. It gets trapped in local minima.

11:05.320 --> 11:19.540
You can choose entirely different baseline shapes, you can swap a Gaussian line shape for a Voight profile, and the software will happily spit out that exact same R-squared of 0.995 while assigning completely different weights to that shoulder.

11:19.980 --> 11:21.760
Or even making it vanish entirely.

11:22.000 --> 11:22.380
Exactly.

11:22.940 --> 11:25.460
The mathematical separation they achieved is non-unique.

11:25.660 --> 11:27.540
