It really looks like they just reverse-engineered the equation.

19:11.400 --> 19:18.400
Like, they knew they needed a 16 terahertz coupling to make the lower branch land on their 71 terahertz mystery shoulder,

19:18.820 --> 19:22.640
so they plugged in whatever absurd density was required to spit that number out,

19:23.020 --> 19:25.040
completely divorced from physical reality.

19:25.460 --> 19:27.220
That's certainly what the math implies.

19:27.600 --> 19:29.920
And the cascading failures in the model don't stop there.

19:30.400 --> 19:37.180
The entire polaraton theory relies on the mitochondrion functioning as a perfectly tuned optical cavity.

19:37.180 --> 19:37.540
Right.

19:37.840 --> 19:41.200
They treat the organelle like a microscopic Fabri-Perot resonator,

19:41.400 --> 19:46.500
where the physical length of the mitochondrion exactly matches the wavelength of the photon,

19:46.600 --> 19:47.880
trapping it in a standing wave.

19:48.280 --> 19:49.680
Like a perfectly tuned organ pipe.

19:49.880 --> 19:50.220
Exactly.

19:50.720 --> 19:58.900
But the preprint claims to observe this precise 71.0 terahertz lower branch across a wide variety of tissues.

19:59.300 --> 20:00.660
Which means different-sized cells.

20:01.060 --> 20:01.380
Yes.

20:01.780 --> 20:05.680
For the kidney and liver cells, the mitochondria are about 2.2 micrometers long.

20:05.680 --> 20:09.980
For the heart and skeletal muscle, they are roughly 1.2 micrometers long.

20:10.260 --> 20:11.420
Wait, the lengths are completely different.

20:11.840 --> 20:14.400
If the length dictates the resonant frequency of the cavity,

20:14.580 --> 20:18.360
how can both lengths support the exact same 87 terahertz photon?

20:18.700 --> 20:19.300
They can't.

20:19.560 --> 20:24.420
If you run the actual cavity equations using the author's own stated lengths and refractive index,

20:25.060 --> 20:30.720
the 2.2 micrometer mitochondria should have a cavity mode up around 90.8 terahertz.

20:30.720 --> 20:31.980
And the smaller ones?

20:32.320 --> 20:36.800
The 1.2 micrometer ones should resonate around 83.3 terahertz.

20:37.060 --> 20:41.460
So they are wildly detuned from the 87 terahertz baseline they actually need.

20:41.800 --> 20:48.340
And because they are detuned, the resulting hybrid branch shouldn't be at a pristine 71.0 terahertz for both tissues.

20:49.020 --> 20:53.100
The kidney cells should show the shoulder at 72.8 terahertz.

20:53.500 --> 20:57.180
The heart cell should show it at 69.0 terahertz.

20:57.180 --> 20:59.200
That is a massive discrepancy.

20:59.600 --> 21:01.000
Nearly 4 terahertz.

21:01.380 --> 21:03.840
That would be blatantly obvious on any infrared spectrum.

21:04.180 --> 21:04.540
Absolutely.

21:05.000 --> 21:08.600
Yet they report seeing the exact same 71.0 feature everywhere.

21:09.220 --> 21:13.020
And biologically, mitochondria aren't factory stamped precision parts anyway.

21:13.420 --> 21:19.400
The preprint itself admits that mitochondrial lengths vary by about 18% within any given tissue sample.

21:19.600 --> 21:22.060
That natural variation has to destroy the signal, right?

21:22.840 --> 21:24.600
Because length dictates frequency.

21:24.600 --> 21:31.320
An 18% variation in length should smear the lower branch across a staggering 14 terahertz range?

21:31.800 --> 21:32.400
Exactly.

21:32.900 --> 21:35.120
You wouldn't see a sharp, distinct shoulder.

21:35.340 --> 21:38.660
You would see a massive, blurred smudge across the entire spectrum.

21:39.540 --> 21:42.240
Flyxion completely traps them in their own logic here.

21:42.860 --> 21:43.300
How so?

21:44.080 --> 21:51.120
Either the mathematical model is evaluated at its stated geometry, which predicts wildly divergent branch positions and massive smearing.

21:51.120 --> 22:01.980
Or the photon is somehow magically forced into an 87 terahertz resonance, regardless of the physical length of the organelle, rendering their entire geometric cavity argument pointless.

22:02.320 --> 22:02.860
Nailed it.

22:03.240 --> 22:07.700
To make matters even worse, Laxion calculates the actual quality of this supposed cavity.

22:08.300 --> 22:10.980
A cavity needs mirrors to bounce the light back and forth, right?

22:11.460 --> 22:12.820
Yeah, to keep the photon trapped.

22:12.820 --> 22:18.580
But the interface between a lipid membrane and the watery cytosol of the cell has terrible reflectivity.

22:19.060 --> 22:28.200
Laxion calculates the Fresnel reflectance based on the refractive index mismatch between lipid and water, and it comes out to a dismal 0.1 to 0.2%.

22:28.200 --> 22:28.620
Oh, wow.

22:28.740 --> 22:35.360
And from that, you derive the Fabry-Perot finesse, which measures how many times a photon can bounce back and forth before escaping.

22:35.360 --> 22:38.560
Okay, so they calculated a finesse of 0.11.

22:39.360 --> 22:41.480
What does that actually mean for the light? Is that good?

22:42.120 --> 22:42.740
It's terrible.

22:43.520 --> 22:50.700
A high finesse cavity is like a room with perfectly parallel mirrors or a perfectly tiled bathroom where a sound echoes continuously.

22:51.120 --> 22:57.780
A finesse of 0.11 is like trying to create a resonant, sustained echo inside a room lined entirely with thick acoustic foam.

22:58.120 --> 22:58.760
Oh, I see.

22:58.960 --> 23:00.120
So it just dies immediately.

23:00.540 --> 23:00.760
Right.

23:00.760 --> 23:05.900
The photon doesn't even complete a single coherent round trip before it leaks out into the surrounding water.

23:06.520 --> 23:10.920
The confinement necessary to sustain a hybrid quantum state simply does not exist.

23:11.260 --> 23:11.500
Okay.

23:11.840 --> 23:12.080
Wow.

23:12.560 --> 23:16.360
So, rung 1 is likely a CO2 artifact.

23:17.380 --> 23:28.520
Rung 2 requires mitochondria made of solid plastic, defies Lorenz oscillator limits, ignores biological size variation, and relies on an optical cavity made of acoustic foam.

23:28.700 --> 23:29.620
That sums it up.

23:29.620 --> 23:36.500
But, you know, we still have to address rungs 3 and 4, because the researchers did perform a biological experiment.

23:36.900 --> 23:37.280
They did.

23:37.280 --> 23:51.380
They took living cells, illuminated them with 10 microwatts of 71 terahertz and 87 terahertz infrared light for 10 minutes, and their fluorescent sensors showed that cellular ATP levels increased by about 10%.

23:51.380 --> 23:56.040
And they concluded this proves the resonance acts as a biological control channel.

23:56.040 --> 23:56.480
Right.

23:56.980 --> 24:03.320
Which brings us to the bathtub analogy, and why Flyxion is so critical of the phrase ATP production.

24:03.720 --> 24:03.960
Yes.

24:04.740 --> 24:10.820
The researchers used a luciferase assay to measure the accumulated concentration of ATP at the end of 10 minutes.

24:10.820 --> 24:19.120
But an accumulated pool of a metabolite is governed by two opposing fluxes, the rate of production minus the rate of consumption.

24:19.480 --> 24:19.880
Right.

24:19.880 --> 24:21.760
It's like a corporate balance sheet.

24:22.120 --> 24:30.640
If I look at a company's bank account at the end of the quarter and see they have 10% more cash on hand than usual, I can't immediately declare they had a record-breaking quarter for sales.

24:30.880 --> 24:31.340
Exactly.

24:31.820 --> 24:35.480
They might have generated the exact same revenue but simply stopped paying their vendors.

24:35.480 --> 24:43.000
So, for the cell, did the infrared light actually turn up the faucet of mitochondrial oxidative phosphorylation?

24:43.540 --> 24:54.060
Or did the light induce a stress response that caused the cell to temporarily halt its energy-consuming processes, thereby plugging the drain and allowing ATP to pool up?

24:54.500 --> 24:58.700
A single endpoint measurement cannot mathematically separate those two realities.

24:58.700 --> 25:03.940
To prove actual production, they would need dynamic real-time measurements, right?

25:04.340 --> 25:12.920
Like extracellular acidification rates, oxygen consumption, or time-resolved fluorescent ATP sensors that show the actual kinetics of the flux.

25:13.340 --> 25:13.780
Exactly.

25:14.380 --> 25:19.040
Without flux measurements, the claim of increased production is entirely speculative.

25:19.700 --> 25:23.620
But Flyxion goes further and examines the physical stress of the illumination itself.

25:23.820 --> 25:24.080
Right.

25:24.340 --> 25:25.060
The heating issue.

25:25.060 --> 25:30.020
The authors claim that 10 microwatts of power is too low to cause significant heating.

25:30.700 --> 25:39.520
Flyxion agrees that if the energy is distributed perfectly across the bulk cluster of cells, the temperature would only rise by a minuscule 0.18 Kelvin.

25:40.000 --> 25:41.480
So they aren't boiling the cells?

25:42.120 --> 25:43.320
Not at the macro level.

25:43.660 --> 25:46.580
But infrared absorption is highly heterogeneous.

25:47.320 --> 25:50.880
Water and lipids absorb energy very differently across these specific frequencies.

25:51.620 --> 25:53.320
Oh, so the heat isn't even.

25:53.320 --> 25:55.820
Right. The energy isn't spreading out evenly.

25:56.180 --> 26:01.540
It's likely being dumped into a very thin, localized layer right at the illuminated surface of the cells.

26:01.960 --> 26:07.560
You could be triggering intense localized thermal spikes that alter membrane fluidity or stress the cell.

26:07.820 --> 26:12.020
Which would immediately alter metabolism and plug that ATP train.

26:12.180 --> 26:12.720
Precisely.

26:12.720 --> 26:26.800
But, you know, even if we assume the heating is perfectly controlled and the light is genuinely plucking a specific molecular string that alters metabolism, does that actually prove the cell uses this mechanism naturally?

26:26.800 --> 26:30.820
And this is rung four, endogenous utilization.

26:31.720 --> 26:34.640
Flyxion handles this with a principle they call proposition three.

26:35.420 --> 26:39.540
Exogenous response does not establish endogenous utilization.

26:40.080 --> 26:47.800
Just because a biological system reacts to an outside intervention does not mean the system naturally utilizes that pathway for internal regulation.

26:48.620 --> 26:49.000
Exactly.

26:49.000 --> 26:54.360
This brings us to the ionizing radiation analogy, which I think perfectly clarifies this fallacy.

26:55.100 --> 26:56.020
It's a great analogy.

26:56.500 --> 27:03.860
If you expose a living cell to heavy doses of gamma rays, the cell will mount a massive, highly specific biological response.

27:03.860 --> 27:06.600
It will activate DNA damage repair pathways.

27:06.960 --> 27:08.440
It will halt its cell cycle.

27:08.720 --> 27:11.360
It will drastically alter its metabolic profile.

27:11.720 --> 27:13.380
The response is totally undeniable.

27:13.740 --> 27:20.360
But absolutely no one observes that reaction and concludes that cells naturally emit gamma rays to communicate with one another.

27:20.560 --> 27:20.740
Right.

27:21.420 --> 27:22.920
The cell is just reacting to trauma.

27:23.680 --> 27:30.000
So just because a system can be perturbed by an external force doesn't mean it's a dedicated regulatory channel.

27:30.000 --> 27:35.840
For a true endogenous communication network to exist, Flyxion outlines three necessary criteria.

27:36.480 --> 27:38.340
U1, an endogenous field.

27:38.700 --> 27:46.660
The cell must actually produce its own 71 terahertz light internally at an amplitude sufficient to be detected above the background noise.

27:47.380 --> 27:50.440
U2, observational covariation.

27:50.740 --> 27:55.340
The ATP levels must naturally fluctuate in tandem with this internal light.

27:55.760 --> 27:57.880
And U3, causal dependence.

27:57.880 --> 28:02.560
You have to prove that neutralizing the internal light source stops the metabolic regulation.

28:03.720 --> 28:06.240
And let me guess, the preprint provides no evidence for any of these?

28:06.500 --> 28:07.260
None whatsoever.

28:08.020 --> 28:11.720
Does a biological body even produce 71 terahertz light naturally?

28:12.000 --> 28:13.120
I mean, I know we emit heat.

28:14.100 --> 28:16.940
It does, but purely as thermal background radiation.

28:17.480 --> 28:24.360
And at 310 Kelvin, human body temperature, the thermal background at 71 terahertz is incredibly sparse.

28:24.360 --> 28:30.780
The mean photon occupation per mode is microscopic, around 1.7 times 10 to the negative 5.

28:31.500 --> 28:33.880
Which means the environment is completely dark at that frequency.

28:34.720 --> 28:39.920
I guess that would be great for a communication channel, because there's no background noise to talk over, but you still need a transmitter.

28:40.340 --> 28:43.680
And this is where the poor cavity quality returns to haunt the model.

28:43.680 --> 28:51.260
The spontaneous emission rate for a vibrating CH2 bond to release an 87 terahertz photon is painfully slow.

28:51.960 --> 28:52.260
How slow?

28:52.760 --> 28:58.140
It would take somewhere between 13 to 145 milliseconds to emit a single photon.

28:58.680 --> 29:04.480
But in a dense, watery, biological environment, a vibrating bond undergoes thermal relaxation,

29:04.860 --> 29:10.580
meaning it bumps into its neighbors and loses its energy as useless heat in approximately one picosecond.

29:11.280 --> 29:12.780
Wait, a picosecond?

29:12.780 --> 29:13.540
Yes.

29:13.940 --> 29:20.300
So the lipid vibration loses its energy as heat billions of times faster than it can manage to broadcast a photon.

29:20.640 --> 29:21.100
Exactly.

29:21.900 --> 29:24.980
It is quite literally the world's worst radio transmitter.

29:25.560 --> 29:28.060
The communication channel is entirely silent.

29:28.600 --> 29:30.900
The physics simply do not permit the transmission.

29:31.560 --> 29:34.340
We've spent a lot of time deconstructing the errors here,

29:34.460 --> 29:38.520
but, you know, this raises a fundamental question about the scientific process itself.

29:39.060 --> 29:39.680
It does.

29:39.680 --> 29:45.400
If the observation is a CO2 ghost, the physics demand plastic mitochondria,

29:45.780 --> 29:49.560
and the biology conflates a stress response with a communication network,

29:49.940 --> 29:55.140
how does a team of highly educated researchers convince themselves they've found a quantum state?

29:55.140 --> 30:01.020
This brings us to what I consider the most philosophically vital part of Flyxion's entire essay,

30:01.180 --> 30:05.900
the distinction between phenomenological modeling and physical reality.

30:06.240 --> 30:08.920
They frame this using the Necker cube illusion.

30:08.920 --> 30:10.980
Oh, the optical illusion?

30:11.540 --> 30:16.640
The two-dimensional wireframe drawing of a cube where your brain flips the perspective back and forth,

30:16.720 --> 30:20.860
making the front face pop to the back and the back face pop to the front?

30:20.860 --> 30:24.900
Exactly. It's a classic example of bistable perception.

30:25.600 --> 30:30.900
Flyxion references a series of fascinating physics papers by researchers like Benedict and Cagliotti,

30:31.120 --> 30:35.880
who mathematically modeled the human brain's perception of the Necker cube using quantum mechanics.

30:36.320 --> 30:36.900
Wait, wait, wait.

30:37.480 --> 30:43.360
They aren't suggesting the human brain is literally utilizing a coherent quantum state to look at a piece of paper, are they?

30:43.360 --> 30:45.720
No, and that is the crucial distinction.

30:46.460 --> 30:52.320
They use a 2x2 quantum Hamiltonian matrix, which happens to be the exact same algebraic structure

30:52.320 --> 30:57.500
utilized by the authors of our mitochondrial preprint, to model the perceptual flipping.

30:58.080 --> 31:00.100
Why use a quantum matrix for psychology?

31:00.780 --> 31:07.680
Because the mathematics of a 2x2 Hamiltonian perfectly describes any system that oscillates between two distinguishable states.

31:08.100 --> 31:13.300
So because the math of the matrix maps perfectly onto the timing of the human brain switching perspectives,

31:14.240 --> 31:16.080
the math works as a descriptive tool.

31:16.340 --> 31:21.900
Precisely. But the researchers modeling the Necker cube are incredibly intellectually honest.

31:22.520 --> 31:26.420
They calculate the effect of action constant for this cognitive flipping,

31:26.420 --> 31:32.360
and they find it as roughly 31 orders of magnitude larger than Planck's constant.

31:33.060 --> 31:38.480
And Planck's constant being the fundamental bedrock value that governs actual microscopic quantum physics.

31:38.480 --> 31:45.060
Right. Because their calculated constant is 31 orders of magnitude too large,

31:45.240 --> 31:50.580
it explicitly marks their mathematical formalism as purely phenomenological.

31:51.240 --> 31:57.600
The variables in their equation have absolutely no microscopic physical quantum interpretation.

31:58.080 --> 32:00.220
It is literally just math.

32:00.220 --> 32:05.260
Yes. The math has what Flyxion calls representational adequacy.

32:05.260 --> 32:08.020
It traces a line that fits the data perfectly.

32:08.660 --> 32:10.880
But it lacks mechanistic identification.

32:11.780 --> 32:14.540
This is the core aha moment of the entire deep dive.

32:15.320 --> 32:19.680
Representational adequacy just means your math algorithm can reproduce the curve on the graph.

32:20.340 --> 32:26.580
Mechanistic identification requires the parameters inside your algorithm to actually match physical reality,

32:26.800 --> 32:29.540
like not having plastic dense mitochondria.

32:29.540 --> 32:30.140
Right.

32:30.660 --> 32:35.520
And it requires the model to make predictions that competing classical models cannot reproduce.

32:36.560 --> 32:43.560
Flyxion formalizes this in Proposition 4, stating that formal equivalence does not imply mechanistic equivalence.

32:44.000 --> 32:50.460
Meaning just because you can fit a 2x2 quantum matrix to your data doesn't mean your physical system is quantum in nature.

32:50.980 --> 32:51.400
Exactly.

32:51.400 --> 32:55.640
To drive this home, Flyxion points out that equation 6 in the preprint,

32:55.840 --> 33:03.800
the exact mathematical equation the authors used to claim the 71 terahertz avoided crossing proves a quantum polariton,

33:04.260 --> 33:09.920
is algebraically identical to the normal mode problem of two classical pendulums tied together by a string.

33:09.920 --> 33:21.320
Wait, are you saying that two grandfather clocks tied together with a shoelace obey the exact same quantum equation they used to claim a new state of cellular life?

33:21.900 --> 33:22.280
Yes.

33:22.280 --> 33:29.780
A classical linear response treatment using basic Lorentz medium physics reproduces the exact same two branches,

33:30.080 --> 33:34.580
the exact same avoided crossing and the exact same square root dependence on density.

33:34.780 --> 33:35.220
Oh, wow.

33:35.220 --> 33:41.040
Even if the authors had successfully proven the physical existence of the 71 terahertz hybrid mode,

33:41.360 --> 33:44.460
all they would have proven is a classical hybrid normal mode.

33:44.880 --> 33:50.200
So, to claim the mantle of quantum biology, you have to demonstrate observables that classical pendulums cannot replicate.

33:50.860 --> 33:55.860
Right, like photon statistics, quantized nonlinear dynamics, true entanglement.

33:56.680 --> 33:58.440
The preprint offers none of this.

33:58.480 --> 34:02.900
They found a mathematical map that vaguely resembled the terrain if you squinted hard enough,

34:03.120 --> 34:05.160
and they declared they had discovered a new continent.

34:05.500 --> 34:06.480
That's a great way to put it.

34:06.580 --> 34:10.340
But, you know, Flyxion's essay doesn't just end with a teardown.

34:10.640 --> 34:11.620
It ends with a roadmap.

34:12.520 --> 34:12.860
Yes.

34:13.380 --> 34:15.300
The counterfactual stress test.

34:15.480 --> 34:16.280
I love this part.

34:16.280 --> 34:20.080
It's what separates great scientific critique from mere skepticism.

34:20.840 --> 34:22.500
It's not enough to say the model is flawed.

34:23.320 --> 34:32.040
You must propose the exact experiments that would force the model to transition from merely accommodating past data to predicting future realities.

34:32.580 --> 34:34.560
Okay, let's walk through these counterfactuals.

34:34.560 --> 34:37.600
Experiment A involves a density shift.

34:38.280 --> 34:46.160
Now, this goes directly back to that problematic mathematical equation where coupling strength relies on the square root of oscillator density.

34:46.620 --> 34:47.040
Exactly.

34:47.920 --> 34:50.160
Flyxion challenges them to intervene on the math.

34:50.900 --> 34:52.800
Don't just accept the theoretical density.

34:53.140 --> 34:54.200
Manipulate it physically.

34:54.200 --> 35:03.680
Use genetic or pharmacological tools to alter the lipid composition of the mitochondrial cristae, literally thinning out the density of those CH2 bonds.

35:04.360 --> 35:04.560
Okay.

35:04.560 --> 35:10.860
So, if you systematically reduce the lipid density to exactly 65.7% of its original state.

35:11.480 --> 35:15.520
The mathematics of their own model dictate an unavoidable physical outcome.

35:16.160 --> 35:23.980
The lower branch, that 71 terahertz mystery shoulder, must physically shift up the spectrum to exactly 74 terahertz.

35:23.980 --> 35:26.700
And here is the true test of biological function.

35:27.020 --> 35:38.700
If you thin out the lipids and the spectral shoulder moves to 74 terahertz, does the peak of the biological ATP response also move in lockstep to 74 terahertz?

35:38.700 --> 35:49.440
Right. If the physics and the biological response move together, exactly as predicted before the measurement was taken, the polariton interpretation gains massive credibility.

35:50.260 --> 35:58.340
But if you thin the lipids and the spectrum shifts to 74, yet the cells still only react when you shine 71 terahertz light on them?

35:58.920 --> 36:00.500
Then the causal link is severed.

36:00.940 --> 36:05.760
The biology is ignoring the polariton, likely because it's just reacting to localized heating.

36:05.760 --> 36:11.640
Experiment A is clever, but experiment B is the absolute gold standard here.

36:12.120 --> 36:13.840
The heavy water lie detector.

36:14.400 --> 36:17.260
This relies on isotopic substitution again, right?

36:17.780 --> 36:19.800
It's a beautifully elegant diagnostic.

36:20.500 --> 36:26.180
Instead of altering the structure or the density, you alter the fundamental chemical identity of the oscillator itself.

36:26.760 --> 36:31.520
You take the lipid CH2 chains and you replace the hydrogen atoms with deuterium.

36:31.520 --> 36:37.980
Deuterium being the heavier isotope of hydrogen, it has an added neutron doubling its mass.

36:38.500 --> 36:41.280
Think of it like a harmonic mass spring equation.

36:41.620 --> 36:44.940
If you put a much thicker, heavier string on a guitar...

36:44.940 --> 36:45.560
The pitch drops.

36:46.060 --> 36:46.420
Exactly.

36:47.080 --> 36:51.620
When you substitute the hydrogen for deuterium, transforming the bonds into CD2,

36:51.620 --> 36:56.580
the increased mass forces the bare vibrational frequency to drop precipitously,

36:57.100 --> 37:01.640
moving from 87 terahertz down to roughly 63.8 terahertz.

37:02.180 --> 37:04.080
And the cavity geometry hasn't changed.

37:04.700 --> 37:06.420
The structural density hasn't changed.

37:06.780 --> 37:08.940
Only the mass of the vibrating atom.

37:09.440 --> 37:14.800
Because the system is now massively detuned, the mathematical prediction is inescapable.

37:14.800 --> 37:19.940
If that 71.0 terahertz feature is a genuine lipid polariton,

37:20.520 --> 37:26.720
the heavier mass forces the lower branch to plunge down the spectrum into the 56 to 62 terahertz range.

37:26.840 --> 37:28.700
It physically must drop.

37:29.340 --> 37:31.900
And if they conduct this deuterium substitution experiment

37:31.900 --> 37:36.800
and the spectral peak remains stubbornly glued to 71.0 terahertz...

37:36.800 --> 37:38.580
Then the game is entirely over.

37:39.120 --> 37:44.320
It proves definitively that the 71.0 terahertz feature has absolutely no relation to the lipids.

37:44.880 --> 37:49.240
Because it's almost certainly the ambient CO2 ghost we discussed back in rung one.

37:49.580 --> 37:49.840
Right.

37:50.120 --> 37:54.840
Because gaseous carbon dioxide in the room doesn't care if the lipids on your slide are heavy or light.

37:55.200 --> 38:00.080
It cleanly and brutally separates a measurement artifact from a biological reality.

38:00.620 --> 38:01.000
Wow.

38:01.000 --> 38:05.980
Finally, Flyxion demands experiment C, the response curve.

38:06.840 --> 38:10.100
The original authors only tested three isolated frequencies, right?

38:10.100 --> 38:15.620
71, 87, and a random 53.7 terahertz control.

38:16.560 --> 38:16.680
Yeah.

38:16.820 --> 38:20.100
And three data points do not constitute a resonance profile.

38:20.800 --> 38:25.620
Flyxion insists they must sweep a finely tunable infrared source across the entire spectrum.

38:25.880 --> 38:26.820
To see the full shape.

38:27.040 --> 38:27.380
Exactly.

38:27.880 --> 38:31.060
If the polariton is a genuine quantum control channel,

38:31.060 --> 38:39.000
the biological ATP response should perfectly trace the precise shape, line width, and symmetry of the spectral absorption feature.

38:39.620 --> 38:46.500
A flat or monotone response curve would indicate the ATP is merely reacting to bulk thermodynamic heating,

38:46.660 --> 38:48.940
not a tightly tuned quantum resonance.

38:48.940 --> 38:53.740
It is deeply satisfying to see the scientific method laid out with this level of rigor.

38:54.600 --> 38:56.900
It isn't about attacking the researchers personally.

38:57.260 --> 39:01.740
It's about holding a proposed mechanism accountable to its own mathematical foundations.

39:02.380 --> 39:02.900
Absolutely.

39:03.780 --> 39:10.000
A theory they can accurately name in advance where a spectral feature will relocate when you swap an isotope.

39:10.540 --> 39:12.900
That is a theory that explains physical reality.

39:12.900 --> 39:21.080
